-type.\n\n### Research Article\n\n# Proofs of three conjectured internal congruences modulo 32 for Schur-type overpartitions\n\nPublished in: Quaestiones Mathematicae\nVolume 48 , issue 4, pages: 611–621\n\nDOI: 10.2989/16073606.2024.2411627\n\nAuthor(s): Weifeng GaoSchool of Mathematical Sciences, Suzhou University of Science and Technology, P.R. China, Olivia X.M. YaoSchool of Mathematical Sciences, Suzhou University of Science and Technology, P.R. China,\n\nKeywords: Primary: Primary: 11P83, Secondary: 05A17, Partitions, Schur-type overpartitions, congruences, theta function identities, (p, k)-parameterization of theta functions,\n\nDownload full text Get new issue alerts\n\n### Abstract\n\nLet S(n) denote the number of overpartitions of Schur-type. Recently, Chern, da Silva and Sellers proved many congruences modulo 8 and 16 for S(n). At the end of their paper, they also posed a conjecture on internal congruences modulo 32 for S(n). In this paper, we confirm their conjecture by using theta function identities and the (p, k)-parameterization of theta functions given by Alaca and Williams. In particular, we show that for any integer j with 0 ≤ j ≤ 31, there are infinitely many integers u_{j} such that S(u_{j} ) ≡ j (mod 32).\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSome distributions on increasing and flattened permutations | Aequationes mathematicae | Springer Nature Link (https://doi.org/10.1007%2Fs00010-026-01275-9)\nciteturn3search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Crawled: last month; ### Theorem 2.1 ... $$\\begin{aligned}&1324, \\quad 1423, \\quad 2134, \\quad 2143, \\quad 2314, \\quad 2413, \\quad 3124, \\quad 3142,\\\\&3214, \\quad 3241, \\quad 3412, \\quad 4123, \\quad 4132, \\quad 4213, \\quad 4231, \\quad 4312. \\end{aligned}$$\n\nDifferentiating this functional equation yields the following differential equation:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned} \\frac{d}{dx} I^{\\textsf {val}}(x,y)= 2I^{\\textsf {val}}(x,y) -1 